Decided: `drover fleet rename <old> <new> [--yes]` re-keys every event row of the old fleet inside one SQLite transaction that commits only after the state files and fleet.toml have moved.
Because: "It applies all the moves above in one transaction: a failure leaves nothing half-renamed, with the backup restored."
Decided: secrets move with their `secret-set` events; drover keeps no Keychain store since #707, and secret files are not per fleet.
Because: crates/core/src/secret.rs:1
Decided: old names resolve by following the logged `fleet-renamed` events in order, so berth→shed→berth still resolves correctly.
Because: "old-name lookups in `status`, `asks`, `board` and `queue ls` resolve to the new fleet"
Decided: owner only means the lane hook refuses `fleet rename` for every lane, conductors included, and also refuses the dry run.
Because: "Owner only: it runs from a run card. Every other caller is refused."
Rejected: renaming worktree folders (premerge-<fleet>, update-<fleet>) — they are git worktrees, so only regular state files move.
Rejected: a config alias table for old names — the event log already records each rename.
Check: a live lane means a running agent named as a lane of an open issue in the old fleet; a pane from a finished lane does not block.
Owner: Pause berth, then run `drover fleet rename berth shed --yes` from a run card; resume shed by hand afterwards.
